# Agent environment — git, shell, paths

## Git on this box

The git harness on this Linux box intermittently **hangs** the call even with
`core.pager=cat` set. Root cause is harness env-inheritance, not git config.
The only reliable fix is a timeout wrapper.

- **Always invoke git via the wrapper.** `git …` raw is forbidden, even with
 `--no-pager`. Use `timeout 30 git …` (or longer for `git log` with ranges).
- **After `git merge --ff-only`, verify with `git log -1 --oneline`.** The
 "Already up to date" message means *the branch ref looks related to the
 source* — not "the merge happened". Compare HEAD to the expected SHA.
- **Worktree-local branch refs lag.** After any merge or fast-forward in the
 operator repo, `git fetch <operator-repo-path>` in every open worktree.
- **Use a fresh shell for every `git` invocation in a subagent.** The working
 tree's shell state (cwd, env) is sticky across `working_directory` overrides
 in the agent harness. Don't chain git commands across `cd` boundaries.
- **No `git log` on the whole tree.** Specify a path; otherwise
 `git --no-pager log -1 --oneline <path>` is the cheap default.

## Paths and python

- **Use absolute python paths.** `.venv/bin/python` will not resolve from the
 wrong cwd after a `working_directory` switch. Use
 `/home/youssef/cursor_setup/Model_Reference_adaptive-controller_UAV/.venv/bin/python`.
- **For new directories, use the `Write` tool.** Chained `mkdir && …` under
 `/tmp/` drops commands silently on this harness. Don't chain.
- **Quote paths containing spaces.** The Windows box has one space in
 `FreeRTOS---Six_Degrees_of_Freedom _Adaptive_controller`; the Linux box
 currently does not, but don't bet on that.

## Push guard — which remote is `origin`

As of 2026-08-14 on this Linux box:

- `origin` = `git@github.com:YoussefChouj/Model_Reference_adaptive-controller_UAV_linux.git` (LINUX)
- `windows` = `git@github.com:YoussefChouj/Model_Reference_adaptive-controller_UAV.git` (WINDOWS, legacy)

If the configured `origin` URL doesn't match the table above, **stop and tell
the user** before any push. Verify with `git remote -v`.

**Rule of thumb:**

- If the commit touches `sim/`, `ground_station/` (linux side), `docs/`,
 `analysis/`, `.cursor/`, `.claude/`, `scripts/`, `pyproject.toml`,
 `requirements.txt`, or the Linux toolchain in `firmware/` → push to `origin`
 (linux).
- If the commit touches `API/`, `FreeRTOS/`, `USER/`, `TASK/`, `BSP/`, `OBJ/`,
 `*.hex`, `*.axf`, `*.uvprojx`, the Keil uVision project, or any
 CMSIS-DAP / pyocd path → those are windows-owned. The Linux box must not
 push firmware changes. Hand them to the operator on the Windows box.

If both kinds of files changed in one commit, **split the commit before
pushing** — never mix platform into a single commit.

## Diagnosis cheatsheet

| Symptom | Most likely cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `git` call returns no exit | Pager / harness hangs | Wrap in `timeout 30 git …` |
| `git push` rejected (non-FF) | Local ahead of remote OR behind merge gate | `git fetch` then check `git status -sb` |
| `Already up to date` but tree unchanged | Working-tree HEAD ≠ branch ref | `git log -1 --oneline` to see real HEAD |
| `mkdir && …` chain drops second command | Silent harness rejection | Use `Write` tool for new files |
| `ModuleNotFoundError` | Wrong Python interpreter | Use full `.venv/bin/python` path |
| `git status --short` returns 113 rows for a one-file edit | `raw/papers/*-images/` regression | `git ls-files raw/papers/ \| grep -c -- "-images/"` — expect 0 |

## Recovery commands (read-only)

```bash
git remote -v                                        # which remote is origin
git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD                      # which branch
git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD@{u}                  # upstream tracking
git log -1 --oneline                                  # real HEAD
git status --short | wc -l                           # working-tree size
git ls-files raw/papers/ | grep -c -- "-images/"     # image drift check
```

If `git ls-files raw/papers/ | grep -c -- "-images/"` returns > 0, the
`-images/` cleanup has regressed. Re-run the cleanup procedure in
`.cursor/rules/000-core.mdc` §History.
